<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  What Android's Auto Backup and device-transfer may take.

  `ChronicleAuth.xml` holds the Plex account token, the server access token and the serialized
  user (cu-108). Those stay on the device: D8 is explicit that auth tokens are not backed up and
  that re-login is expected on restore. Backups are end-to-end encrypted with the device screen
  lock on Android 9+, so including them would not have been an open leak, but a token restored
  onto hardware whose owner has not authenticated to Plex is exactly what D8 rules out.

  Auto Backup can exclude a preferences **file** but not individual keys, which is why the
  credentials now live in a file of their own. Before cu-108 they shared `Chronicle.xml` with the
  settings, so the only correct rule was to exclude the whole thing — and the harmless settings
  were collateral. Now `Chronicle.xml` is **allowed**, so preferences the user has set survive a
  device transfer while the credentials do not.

  The Room databases are still excluded. They hold only what Plex can re-derive — books, tracks,
  chapters, collections — plus listening progress, which also lives server-side and is synced
  (cu-9/cu-14). Restoring a stale copy onto a fresh install would fight that sync rather than help
  it, and the export in cu-17/cu-77 is the supported way to move local-only state.

  Note `device-transfer` is deliberately as strict as `cloud-backup`: a direct device-to-device
  copy still moves a token onto hardware whose owner has not authenticated to Plex.

  Keep this file and `backup_rules.xml` in agreement; `BackupRulesTest` fails the build otherwise,
  because a rule that applies on only some API levels is the kind of gap that stays invisible
  until it matters.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
  <cloud-backup>
    <exclude
      domain="sharedpref"
      path="ChronicleAuth.xml" />
    <exclude domain="database" />
  </cloud-backup>

  <device-transfer>
    <exclude
      domain="sharedpref"
      path="ChronicleAuth.xml" />
    <exclude domain="database" />
  </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
